Description: Infers, for every cell of a female single-cell RNA-seq sample,
    which X chromosome is inactive. Allele-specific UMIs at heterozygous
    SNVs (from STAR alignments in WASP mode) are phased into two haplotypes
    by a parallel multi-start optimiser with optional co-segregation
    pretraining, and each cell is called X1, X2, biallelic (Both),
    Low_coverage or Unknown. Escape candidates and monoallelic SNVs are
    handled explicitly. EXCISE extends XCISE (Henning et al. 2024); the
    implementation is a C++ port of excise1.5.pl built on htslib (Rhtslib).
